{"tool_name":"timiner","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"timiner","home":"http://icbi.i-med.ac.at/software/timiner/timiner.shtml","summary":"NGS data mining pipeline for cancer immunology and immunotherapy","addition_date":"2018-06-12T18:49:49Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:40:18.920607Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:timiner","credit":[{"email":"zlatko.trajanoski@i-med.ac.at","name":"Zlatko Trajanoski","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://icbi.i-med.ac.at/software/timiner/doc/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3092"},{"term":"Sequence feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0253"}]}],"name":"TIminer","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx377","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: Recently, a number of powerful computational tools for dissecting tumor-immune cell interactions from next-generation sequencing data have been developed. However, the assembly of analytical pipelines and execution of multi-step workflows are laborious and involve a large number of intermediate steps with many dependencies and parameter settings. Here we present TIminer, an easy-to-use computational pipeline for mining tumor-immune cell interactions from next-generation sequencing data. TIminer enables integrative immunogenomic analyses, including: human leukocyte antigens typing, neoantigen prediction, characterization of immune infiltrates and quantification of tumor immunogenicity.","authors":[{"name":"Charoentong P."},{"name":"Finotello F."},{"name":"Mayer C."},{"name":"Rieder D."},{"name":"Tappeiner E."},{"name":"Trajanoski Z."}],"citationCount":73,"date":"2017-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"TIminer: NGS data min